[{"answer":"OK, Jack. Before we plan our presentation about refrigeration,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/1.mp3"},{"answer":"let's discuss what we've discovered so far.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/2.mp3"},{"answer":"Fine, Annie.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/3.mp3"},{"answer":"Though I have to admit I haven't done much research yet.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/4.mp3"},{"answer":"Nor me.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/5.mp3"},{"answer":"But I found an interesting article about icehouses.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/6.mp3"},{"answer":"I'd seen some 18th- and 19th-century ones here in the UK,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/7.mp3"},{"answer":"so I knew they were often built in a shady area or underground,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/8.mp3"},{"answer":"close to lakes that might freeze in the winter.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/9.mp3"},{"answer":"Then blocks of ice could be cut and stored in the icehouse.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/10.mp3"},{"answer":"But I didn't realise that insulating the blocks with straw or sawdust meant they didn't melt for months.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/11.mp3"},{"answer":"The ancient Romans had refrigeration, too.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/12.mp3"},{"answer":"I didn't know that.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/13.mp3"},{"answer":"Yes, pits were dug in the ground,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/14.mp3"},{"answer":"and snow was imported from the mountains -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/15.mp3"},{"answer":"even though they were at quite a distance.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/16.mp3"},{"answer":"The snow was stored in the pits.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/17.mp3"},{"answer":"Ice formed at the bottom of it.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/18.mp3"},{"answer":"Both the ice and the snow were then sold.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/19.mp3"},{"answer":"The ice cost more than the snow","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/20.mp3"},{"answer":"and my guess is that only the wealthy members of society could afford it.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/21.mp3"},{"answer":"I wouldn't be surprised.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/22.mp3"},{"answer":"I also came across an article about modern domestic fridges.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/23.mp3"},{"answer":"Several different technologies are used,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/24.mp3"},{"answer":"but they were too complex for me to understand.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/25.mp3"},{"answer":"You have to wonder what happens when people get rid of old ones.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/26.mp3"},{"answer":"You mean because the gases in them are harmful for the environment?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/27.mp3"},{"answer":"Exactly.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/28.mp3"},{"answer":"At least there are now plenty of organisations that will recycle most of the components safely,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/29.mp3"},{"answer":"but of course some people just dump old fridges in the countryside.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/30.mp3"},{"answer":"It's hard to see how they can be stopped unfortunately.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/31.mp3"},{"answer":"In the UK we get rid of three million a year altogether!","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/32.mp3"},{"answer":"That sounds a lot, especially because fridges hardly ever break down.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/33.mp3"},{"answer":"That's right.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/34-2024-11-04-00-55-23.mp3"},{"answer":"In this country we keep domestic fridges for 11 years on average,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/35.mp3"},{"answer":"and a lot last for 20 or more.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/36.mp3"},{"answer":"So if you divide the cost by the number of years you can use a fridge, they're not expensive,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/37.mp3"},{"answer":"compared with some household appliances.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/38.mp3"},{"answer":"True.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/39.mp3"},{"answer":"I suppose manufacturers encourage people to spend more by making them different colours and designs.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/40.mp3"},{"answer":"I'm sure when my parents bought their first fridge they had hardly any choice!","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/41.mp3"},{"answer":"Yes, there's been quite a change.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/42.mp3"},{"answer":"Right, let's make a list of topics to cover in our presentation,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/43.mp3"},{"answer":"and decide who's going to do more research on them.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/44-2024-11-04-00-59-29.mp3"},{"answer":"Then later, we can get together and plan the next step.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/45.mp3"},{"answer":"OK.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/46.mp3"},{"answer":"How about starting with how useful refrigeration is,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/47.mp3"},{"answer":"and the range of goods that are refrigerated nowadays?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/48.mp3"},{"answer":"Because of course it's not just food and drinks.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/49.mp3"},{"answer":"No, I suppose flowers and medicines are refrigerated, too.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/50.mp3"},{"answer":"And computers.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/51.mp3"},{"answer":"I could do that, unless you particularly want to.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/52.mp3"},{"answer":"No, that's fine by me.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/53-2024-11-04-01-01-27.mp3"},{"answer":"What about the effects of refrigeration on people's health?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/54.mp3"},{"answer":"After all, some of the chemicals used in the 19th century were pretty harmful,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/55.mp3"},{"answer":"but there have been lots of benefits too,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/56.mp3"},{"answer":"like always having access to fresh food.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/57.mp3"},{"answer":"Do you fancy dealing with that?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/58.mp3"},{"answer":"I'm not terribly keen, to be honest.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/59.mp3"},{"answer":"Nor me.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/60.mp3"},{"answer":"My mind just goes blank when I read anything about chemicals.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/61.mp3"},{"answer":"Oh, all right then, I'll do you a favour.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/62.mp3"},{"answer":"But you owe me, Jack.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/63.mp3"},{"answer":"OK.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/64.mp3"},{"answer":"What about the effects on food producers,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/65.mp3"},{"answer":"like farmers in poorer countries being able to export their produce to developed countries?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/66.mp3"},{"answer":"Something for you, maybe?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/67.mp3"},{"answer":"I don't mind. It should be quite interesting.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/68.mp3"},{"answer":"I think we should also look at how refrigeration has helped whole cities - like Las Vegas,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/69.mp3"},{"answer":"which couldn't exist without refrigeration","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/70.mp3"},{"answer":"because it's in the middle of a desert.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/71-2024-11-04-01-06-25.mp3"},{"answer":"Right.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/72.mp3"},{"answer":"I had a quick look at an economics book in the library that's got a chapter about this sort of thing.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/73.mp3"},{"answer":"I could give you the title, if you want to do this section.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/74.mp3"},{"answer":"Not particularly, to be honest.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/75.mp3"},{"answer":"I find economics books pretty heavy going, as a rule.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/76.mp3"},{"answer":"OK, leave it to me, then.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/77.mp3"},{"answer":"Thanks.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/78.mp3"},{"answer":"Then there's transport,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/79.mp3"},{"answer":"and the difference that refrigerated trucks have made.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/80.mp3"},{"answer":"I wouldn't mind having a go at that.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/81.mp3"},{"answer":"Don't forget trains, too.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/82.mp3"},{"answer":"I read something about milk and butter being transported in refrigerated railroad cars in the USA,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/83.mp3"},{"answer":"right back in the 1840s.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/84.mp3"},{"answer":"I hadn't thought of trains. Thanks.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/85.mp3"},{"answer":"Shall we have a separate section on domestic fridges?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/86.mp3"},{"answer":"After all, they're something everyone's familiar with.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/87.mp3"},{"answer":"What about splitting it into two?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/88.mp3"},{"answer":"You could investigate 19th- and 20th-century fridges,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/89.mp3"},{"answer":"and I'll concentrate on what's available these days,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/90.mp3"},{"answer":"and how manufacturers differentiate their products from those of their competitors.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/91.mp3"},{"answer":"OK, that'd suit me.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-15-test-4-part-3-2023-01-19-23-42-10/92.mp3"}]
